{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "JOB",
  "chapter": 28,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "JOB.28.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.28.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Surely there is a vein for the silver, and a place for gold ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "where",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " they fine ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.28.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.28.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Iron is taken out of the earth, and brass ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " melted ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "out of",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the stone.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.28.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.28.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He setteth an end to darkness, and searcheth out all perfection: the stones of darkness, and the shades of death.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.28.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.28.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The flood breaketh out from the inhabitant: ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "even the waters",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " forgotten by the foot: they are dried up, they have gone away from men.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.28.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.28.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "As for",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the earth, out of it cometh bread: and under it is turned up as it were fire.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.28.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.28.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The stones of it ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the place of sapphires: and it hath dust of gold.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.28.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.28.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "There is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a path which no fowl knoweth, and which the vultur's eye hath not seen:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.28.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.28.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The lion's whelps have not trodden it, nor the fierce lion passed by it.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.28.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.28.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He putteth forth his hand upon the rock; he overturneth the mountains by the roots.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.28.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.28.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He cutteth out rivers among the rocks; and his eye seeth every precious thing.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.28.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.28.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He bindeth the floods from overflowing; and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "the thing that is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " hid he bringeth forth to light.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.28.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.28.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But where shall wisdom be found? and where ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the place of understanding?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.28.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.28.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Man knoweth not the price of it; neither is it found in the land of the living.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.28.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.28.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The depth saith, It ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not in me: and the sea saith, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "It is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not with me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.28.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.28.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "It cannot be obtained for gold, neither shall silver be weighed ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "for",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the price of it.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.28.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.28.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "It cannot be valued with the gold of Ophir, with the precious onyx, or the sapphire.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.28.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.28.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The gold and the crystal cannot equal it: and the exchange of it ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "shall not be for",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " jewels of fine gold.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.28.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.28.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "No mention shall be made of coral, or of pearls: for the price of wisdom ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " above rubies.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.28.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.28.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The topaz of Cush shall not equal it, neither shall it be valued with pure gold.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.28.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.28.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Whence then cometh wisdom? and where ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the place of understanding?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.28.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.28.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Seeing it is hid from the eyes of all living, and kept close from the fowls of the air.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.28.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.28.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Destruction and death say, We have heard the fame of it with our ears.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.28.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.28.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "God understandeth the way of it, and he knoweth its place.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.28.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.28.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For he looketh to the ends of the earth, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " seeth under the whole heaven;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.28.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.28.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "To make the weight for the winds; and he weigheth the waters by measure.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.28.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.28.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When he made a decree for the rain, and a way for the lightning of the thunder:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.28.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.28.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then did he see it, and declare it; he prepared it, yea, and searched it out.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.28.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.28.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And to man he said, Behold, the fear of the LORD, that ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " wisdom; and to depart from evil ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " understanding.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
